{189}{Ahh, you do not know, do you? A'er-N'es and N'es-R'din in the ancient tongues. Do you see? A'er-N'es. "A'er" loosely translated would be "after the lineage of". It is obvious, is it not? Arronax was Nasrudin's son, yesss?}{Ahh, you do not know, do you? A'er-N'es and N'es-R'din in the ancient tongues. Do you see? A'er-N'es. "A'er" loosely translated would be "after the lineage of". It is obvious, is it not? Arronax was Nasrudin's son, yesss?}{}{20}{}{ru2111 }
{190}{So what are you doing to bring Arronax back?}{}{5}{}{71}{ }
{191}{I'm overcome with grief by your tale. I must be going.}{}{5}{qa1027 1, gf2027 0}{-7}{ }
{194}{The training of years enabled me to attempt to cast my mind into the Void. Tens of years brought me nothing but silence, until the wards were weakened enough to let my mind touch the master's. Confusion muddied our link at first, but it soon became strong.}{The training of years enabled me to attempt to cast my mind into the Void. Tens of years brought me nothing but silence, until the wards were weakened enough to let my mind touch the master's. Confusion muddied our link at first, but it soon became strong.}{}{21}{}{ }
